 above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 8.4 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.2 to 5.8. December accounts for 7% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 15% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,608.99 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows that some contracts are just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices may be low, budgets fixed, or needs separate. Statistical patterns don't indicate improper actions.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts awarded in December. Look at awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same service. Review if multiple contracts cover the same need to ensure no overlap or duplication.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["8pcGIj7p2U9SYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D","6B9twEJUh1t6nTs9LZ9RhQ%3D%3D","dt3nvvpFiemP%2Bo96UAV7cQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}